# The test fleet's MacBook Pro (M1 Pro, 16 GB) on macOS 26.6.2. sysctl,
# sw_vers and system_profiler are in their real formats; identifying fields
# are REDACTED. Confirmed against the machine on 2026-09-18: the advisor's
# own run there (scripts/verify.command, build 4e34907) read Metal's
# recommendedMaxWorkingSetSize as 12713115648 bytes (11.84 GiB, the "11.8 GiB"
# Ollama v0.34.2 logs), with iogpu.wired_limit_mb unset — the value below —
# and the same OS build, core counts, memory and 16-core GPU. The real
# profile matches testdata/golden/AppleSiliconM1Pro.json except for the
# hostname, the home folder and free disk space.
-- $ sysctl --
hw.memsize: 17179869184
hw.physicalcpu: 10
hw.logicalcpu: 10
machdep.cpu.brand_string: Apple M1 Pro
hw.optional.arm64: 1
sysctl.proc_translated: 0
iogpu.wired_limit_mb: 0
-- $ sw_vers --
ProductName:		macOS
ProductVersion:		26.6.2
BuildVersion:		25G83
-- $ system_profiler --
